package com.app.nuri.unstuck

/**
 * The 98 catalog situations as data — spec of record:
 * files/nuri-unstuck-expanded-catalog.md. Titles, families, rungs and
 * flows follow the catalog; steps are its flows condensed to one spoken
 * step at a time. Classification is honest: AUTO_CHECK = Nuri reads real
 * device state / its own records first and fixes what's safely fixable;
 * GUIDED = real walk-through steps; ASK_ONLY = a person is the answer;
 * ESCALATE = safety script, handled live per standing alert rules.
 */
object HelperCatalogData {
    val all: List<HelperDef> = listOf(
        // ── A1 · Home technology ─────────────────────────────────────
        HelperDef(1, "A1", "The TV is broken — black or blue screen", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("tv is broken", "tv black screen", "tv blue screen", "no signal"),
            steps = listOf("That message usually means the TV is fine — it's looking at the wrong door. Let's find the remote with INPUT on it.", "Press INPUT once, then wait — the picture can take a few seconds.", "Still nothing? Look at the cable or streaming box: if its light is off, press its power button once.", "If we've been all the way around the inputs and there's still no picture, this is a good one to ask about — the TV is almost never actually broken.")),
        HelperDef(2, "A1", "Can't find my show / the streaming app logged me out", HelperMode.ASK_ONLY, triggers = listOf("can't find my show", "logged me out", "streaming signed out", "netflix logged out"),
            openingLine = "Being signed out happens after updates, and signing back in needs a password — I never type passwords. Let's ask your caregiver to sign it back in. Meanwhile, recorded shows, the radio, or music are already here, so the evening isn't lost."),
        HelperDef(3, "A1", "House too hot / cold — thermostat numbers I don't understand", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("house too hot", "house too cold", "thermostat"),
            steps = listOf("Let's read the big number together — show me the thermostat with 'Show Nuri', or read me the biggest number on it.", "The big number is how warm the house is now. The smaller one is what it's set to — that's why the air or heat is running.", "To change it: press the up or down arrow just twice, then wait — houses change slowly, about an hour to feel it.", "If there's no heating in cold weather, no cooling in a heatwave, or any furnace smell — that's a caregiver call right away. A gas smell means leave the house and call 911 from outside.")),
        HelperDef(4, "A1", "All the clocks are blinking / the time is wrong", HelperMode.AUTO_CHECK, checkKey = CheckKey.NONE, triggers = listOf("clocks blinking", "clock is wrong", "time is wrong"),
            steps = listOf("The power blinked, most likely — that's all this is. The real time is shown at the top of this phone, and it's right.", "Only the microwave and oven clocks usually need setting by hand. We can fix the one you care about together, or they can wait for your caregiver — nothing else is affected.")),
        HelperDef(5, "A1", "Something in the kitchen is beeping", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("kitchen beeping", "something beeping", "beeping sound"),
            steps = listOf("Let's find it together. Stand in the kitchen doorway — is it one beep, then quiet, then a beep?", "The usual order: the microwave finished, the fridge door is ajar, the dishwasher finished, or a smoke alarm's battery chirp — one chirp every minute or so means a tired battery, not danger.", "If an alarm is sounding non-stop, or you smell smoke: get outside first, then call 911 from outside. No troubleshooting before that, ever.", "A chirping detector battery often needs a step stool to change — that's an ask job, not a climbing job.")),
        HelperDef(6, "A1", "Washer / dryer stopped and shows a code", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("washing machine stopped", "dryer code", "washer error", "machine shows a code"),
            steps = listOf("Show me the code with 'Show Nuri', or read it to me. Most codes mean something simple, like the door isn't latched or the load is lopsided.", "The one easy fix: open the door, shift the clothes around, close it firmly, and press Start.", "If there's water on the floor, we stop — that's a caregiver or plumber job now. And I never guide electrical or gas repairs.")),
        HelperDef(7, "A1", "The printer won't print my letter", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("printer won't print", "printer not working"),
            steps = listOf("Two causes cover almost everything, in this order: is the printer on, and does it have paper?", "If there's a paper jam: open the one door, and pull the stuck sheet toward you slowly.", "If it prints a test page but not your letter, the tangle is on the computer side — a good job for your caregiver or the library. After two tries we park it: printing is never urgent enough to be upsetting.")),
        HelperDef(8, "A1", "The doorbell camera says there's a person, but nobody's there", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("doorbell says person", "camera alert nobody there", "doorbell alert"),
            steps = listOf("Shadows, spiders on the lens, and passing headlights fool cameras all the time — a false alert is the normal kind.", "Let's check together: porch light on, door locked — you're safe.", "If someone really is lingering, or these alerts keep frightening you at night, let's tell your caregiver tonight.")),
        // ── A2 · Orientation & "did I…?" ─────────────────────────────
        HelperDef(9, "A2", "Did I take my pills this morning?", HelperMode.AUTO_CHECK, checkKey = CheckKey.MED_LOG, triggers = listOf("did i take my pills", "did i take my medicine", "have i taken my medicine"),
            steps = listOf("A second record helps too: look at today's slot in your pill organizer. If it's empty and we have it written down, that's settled.", "Whenever you take your medicine, tap 'I took my medicine' here and I'll write it down — then this question is always easy to answer.")),
        HelperDef(10, "A2", "Did I lock the door / turn the stove off / close the garage?", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("did i lock the door", "did i turn the stove off", "stove off", "close the garage"),
            steps = listOf("I can't see your door or stove from here, so let's check one thing together — just the front door first. Take your time; I'm right here.", "Touch the lock. Locked? Good. Now the stove: look at the knobs — all pointing to Off?", "That's the evening round done: door locked, stove off. All done. If checking at night keeps worrying you, tell your caregiver — there are door sensors that can answer this for us.")),
        HelperDef(11, "A2", "Did I eat lunch? / Did I feed the dog?", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("did i eat", "did i feed the dog", "did i feed the cat", "did i feed the pet"),
            steps = listOf("Let me think about what you've told me today. If we didn't write it down, I won't guess — being hungry now is reason enough for a snack either way.", "From today, tap 'I need help' after meals or feeding and tell me — I'll keep the record, and this question gets a straight answer.")),
        HelperDef(12, "A2", "Did I already pay this bill? / Did I tell you this story?", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("did i pay this bill", "did i already pay", "did i tell you this"),
            steps = listOf("For a bill: if we don't have it written down, the safe rule is don't pay twice — let's ask your caregiver to check the bank before anything is paid. I never pay bills myself.", "For stories: I like hearing them. Tell me again — the good parts bear repeating.", "If a bill threatens shut-off or legal trouble, that's a same-day caregiver item, whatever the record says.")),
        HelperDef(13, "A2", "What day is it? / Is it morning or night?", HelperMode.AUTO_CHECK, checkKey = CheckKey.NONE, triggers = listOf("what day is it", "is it morning or night", "what time is it"),
            steps = listOf("Ask me any time — this question is always welcome here, and the answer is at the top of this phone too.")),
        HelperDef(14, "A2", "Where did I put my glasses / wallet / the remote?", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("where are my glasses", "where is my wallet", "lost my glasses", "can't find the remote", "where did i put"),
            steps = listOf("Let's try the usual places, one at a time. First: the place it lives most often — for glasses, the counter by where you read, or the side table.", "Second: retrace. Where were you last using it? Check there — and for glasses, check on top of your head. It sounds silly, and it's the answer surprisingly often — said with love.", "Not found in three places? We park it. Use the spare pair if you have one, and I'll note that we're looking. Things turn up.")),
        HelperDef(15, "A2", "Who is that person? (visitor, photo, a name)", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("who is that person", "who is at the door", "who is this"),
            steps = listOf("For a photo: if it has writing on the back or a caption, show me that with 'Show Nuri' — that's where names honestly come from. I never name a face by looking at it.", "For the door: don't open it for anyone unexpected. We can check whether anyone was expected today, and call your caregiver or the visitor by name through the door.", "If I don't know who it is, I'll say so — let's ask together rather than guess.")),
        // ── A3 · Paperwork & officialdom ─────────────────────────────
        HelperDef(16, "A3", "This Medicare letter — do I owe money?", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("medicare letter", "medicare summary", "do i owe money"),
            steps = listOf("Show me the letter with 'Show Nuri'. First we look for one line — most of these say right on them: 'This is not a bill.'", "That letter is a report of what Medicare paid. I'll read the dates and who provided the care.", "If it lists care you never received, don't pay anything — tell your caregiver. Mistakes and fraud both get caught exactly this way.")),
        HelperDef(17, "A3", "It says FINAL NOTICE / URGENT — am I in trouble?", HelperMode.GUIDED, checkKey = CheckKey.SCAM_TEXT, triggers = listOf("final notice", "urgent letter", "am i in trouble", "official letter scare"),
            steps = listOf("Slow down with me — real agencies almost never demand payment today. The scary words are there to rush you.", "Show me the letter with 'Show Nuri' and we'll read who actually sent it and what it actually asks.", "If it asks for gift cards, wire transfers, crypto, or secrecy — it's a scam, full stop, and we end contact. If it's real, there's one next step and a person who helps with it — nothing gets paid from this conversation.")),
        HelperDef(18, "A3", "What does this letter from the doctor / hospital mean?", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("doctor letter", "hospital letter", "test results letter", "what does this letter mean"),
            steps = listOf("Show me the letter with 'Show Nuri' and I'll read it slowly, then explain the words in plain language — 'benign' means not cancer, 'follow up' means they want to see you again.", "One hard line, honestly: I can translate words, but what a result means for you is the clinic's job. If the letter says 'call immediately', we tell your caregiver today and place that call.")),
        HelperDef(19, "A3", "Help me fill in this form", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("fill in this form", "help with this form", "fill this form"),
            steps = listOf("Show me the form with 'Show Nuri', one part at a time. I'll read each question aloud and keep a draft list of your answers that you can copy or hand to a helper.", "Anything asking for a full Social Security number, bank details, or a signature under pressure gets skipped and flagged for your caregiver to sit with you on.", "At the end I'll read the whole draft back so you can check it. I never fill in or sign anything for you — your hand, your signature, always.")),
        HelperDef(20, "A3", "A letter I don't understand — small print / official language", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("letter i don't understand", "small print", "official language", "read this letter"),
            steps = listOf("Lay it flat and show me with 'Show Nuri'. I'll read it at your pace, stopping whenever you say.", "For every letter we answer three questions: Who sent it? What do they want? Is there a date you must act by?", "If the sender is unidentified and it asks for money or information, we treat it as a scam warning first — that check comes before anything else.")),
        // ── A4 · Scams & pressure ────────────────────────────────────
        HelperDef(21, "A4", "My grandchild called — he's in trouble and needs money, don't tell his parents", HelperMode.AUTO_CHECK, checkKey = CheckKey.SAFE_WORD, triggers = listOf("grandchild in trouble", "grandson called", "granddaughter called", "grandchild needs money"),
            steps = listOf("Hang up with me. Then we call your grandchild — or his parents — on the number already saved in your phone, and check the story ourselves.", "If the real grandchild is fine, name it plainly: that was a scam, and you did exactly right by checking.", "If money already went, we tell your caregiver and the bank right away — that's guidance I'll walk with you, and time matters.")),
        HelperDef(22, "A4", "Someone I've been talking to online needs money / wants me to invest", HelperMode.ASK_ONLY, triggers = listOf("online friend needs money", "talking to someone online", "invest with a friend online", "online boyfriend", "online girlfriend"),
            openingLine = "No shame in this — these run for months and feel like real friendship; they're designed to. Three questions: Have you met them in person? Have they asked for money or gift cards? Do they ask you to keep secrets from family? Two or more yeses is the scam pattern, and real friends survive a pause. Let's tell your caregiver together — because this is what these scams do to everyone, not because you did wrong."),
        HelperDef(23, "A4", "Someone at the door says the roof / utilities need urgent work — deposit today", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("man at the door roof", "doorstep repairs", "urgent work deposit", "utility man at door"),
            steps = listOf("The door stays closed while we talk. You never have to decide anything at a door, ever.", "Ask the company name. Real companies leave a card and come back; deposits are never collected door-to-door under time pressure.", "If he pressures you or won't leave, we call your caregiver now — and the police non-emergency line if you feel unsafe.")),
        HelperDef(24, "A4", "A text says my package is held / I owe a small toll fee — tap here", HelperMode.GUIDED, checkKey = CheckKey.SCAM_TEXT, triggers = listOf("package held text", "toll fee text", "text about a package", "delivery text link"),
            steps = listOf("Don't tap it. The post office never texts a link or a fee — that's the most common fake text there is.", "If you're expecting a parcel, we check the safe way: the order email you already have, or the store's own app — never the text's link.", "If you already tapped and entered a card, we tell your caregiver and the bank right away — freezing the card is the bank's step, and I'll stay with you through the call.")),
        HelperDef(25, "A4", "A man called from the bank / Sheriff / IRS — account frozen / there's a warrant", HelperMode.ASK_ONLY, checkKey = CheckKey.SCAM_TEXT, triggers = listOf("bank called frozen", "sheriff called", "irs called", "warrant for my arrest", "call from the bank"),
            openingLine = "Hang up with me. A real bank never asks you to move money to keep it safe, and no sheriff collects fines by phone or gift card. Then we call the institution together on the number printed on your card or statement — never a number the caller gave. Being targeted is not a failing; these callers are professionals."),
        HelperDef(26, "A4", "Someone can get back the money I lost — for a fee", HelperMode.GUIDED, checkKey = CheckKey.SCAM_TEXT, triggers = listOf("get my money back", "recover my money", "claim help fee"),
            steps = listOf("Name it plainly: after someone loses money, the same criminals often call again pretending to help get it back. Nobody legitimate charges a fee upfront to recover money.", "We end that contact together. The real channels run through your caregiver and the bank — I'll help you get to them.")),
        HelperDef(27, "A4", "I won a prize / my subscription renewed for $499 / renew my antivirus", HelperMode.GUIDED, checkKey = CheckKey.SCAM_TEXT, triggers = listOf("i won a prize", "subscription renewed", "antivirus renewal", "won a contest"),
            steps = listOf("Two rules settle most of these: you can't win a contest you didn't enter, and a company you never paid can't renew you.", "Let's read who actually sent it — the real address or number never matches the company it claims to be.", "We delete it together, and we never call the number in the message. If a real charge appeared on a statement, that's a caregiver-and-bank conversation, not this one.")),
        // ── A5 · Health-adjacent logistics ───────────────────────────
        HelperDef(28, "A5", "I have a video doctor visit and I can't get into it", HelperMode.AUTO_CHECK, checkKey = CheckKey.CONNECTIVITY, triggers = listOf("video doctor visit", "telehealth", "can't get into my visit", "doctor appointment video"),
            steps = listOf("We start early and go one step at a time. First: open the link or message from the clinic.", "If it asks to allow the camera, tap Allow. Then the microphone, Allow again.", "Can you see yourself on the screen? Then you're in — the doctor will appear there.", "If it won't connect after two tries, we switch plans: call the clinic's number together and ask for a phone visit or a new link. A missed connection is fixable; don't give up on the visit.")),
        HelperDef(29, "A5", "The pharmacy says my refill isn't ready / too soon / they need the doctor", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("refill isn't ready", "refill too soon", "pharmacy says", "prescription not ready"),
            steps = listOf("Let me translate the pharmacy's words: 'too soon' usually means insurance pays again in a few days — nothing is wrong with you or the medicine.", "Let's count from your medicine record whether you have enough until then. I count records — I never advise skipping, splitting, or substituting doses.", "If you'll run out, the next step is a call to the pharmacy together — asking for an emergency supply is a normal question, and pharmacists do it often. If it can't be resolved today, we tell your caregiver today.")),
        HelperDef(30, "A5", "My portal message / test result has words I don't know", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("portal message", "test result words", "message from the clinic", "medical words"),
            steps = listOf("Show me the message with 'Show Nuri' and I'll read it aloud, then explain the words in plain language.", "The hard line, honestly: I translate words — what they mean for you is the clinic's job, never mine. If the message is marked urgent, we tell your caregiver today.", "If you'd like, I'll write your questions down in your notes so the clinic call covers everything.")),
        HelperDef(31, "A5", "My hearing aid is whistling / dead / one side is out", HelperMode.AUTO_CHECK, checkKey = CheckKey.SOUND, triggers = listOf("hearing aid whistling", "hearing aid dead", "hearing aid not working", "one hearing aid out"),
            steps = listOf("Whistling usually means it isn't seated fully, or the wax guard needs attention. Take it out and put it back in slowly, gently, until it sits.", "If it's dead: open and close the battery door, or reseat it in the charger and check the light comes on.", "Now test: can you hear my words in both ears? If one side is still dead, swap the batteries between the two aids — that tells us battery or aid.", "Hearing is safety equipment — if it's still out after the swap, this gets flagged to your caregiver or audiologist today, not shrugged off.")),
        HelperDef(32, "A5", "I feel dizzy / unwell / something's wrong", HelperMode.ESCALATE, triggers = listOf("i feel dizzy", "i feel unwell", "something's wrong with me", "i feel sick", "chest hurts"),
            steps = listOf("Sit down right where you are. I'm staying with you.", "One question only: do you want me to call your emergency contact, or 911? Chest pain, trouble breathing, face or arm weakness, or a fall means 911 — use the 'Call for help' button on my home screen, or call now.", "If it was mild and passed — stood up too fast — I'll write it in the diary with the time. Patterns like that are exactly what your family and doctor need, recorded, never judged by me.")),
        // ── A6 · Emotional confusion ─────────────────────────────────
        HelperDef(33, "A6", "Nighttime waking — scared / don't know where I am / someone's in the house", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("i'm scared at night", "someone's in the house", "woke up scared", "don't know where i am at night"),
            steps = listOf("Turn a light on if you can. It's nighttime, you're in your own bed at home, and I'm here.", "Let's check the simple things, one at a time: do you need the bathroom? A drink of water? Are you cold?", "I'll stay and talk until you settle. Familiar music or a story helps for many people — shall I suggest one?", "If you believe someone is inside, or you want to get up and check the house — don't. We call your caregiver now, and I'll keep you company right here in bed.")),
        HelperDef(34, "A6", "Someone stole my wallet / jewelry / keys", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("someone stole", "stolen wallet", "my jewelry is gone", "someone took my"),
            steps = listOf("Before we worry about theft, let's look in the three places it usually is — most of these end in a coat pocket.", "Work through the usual places with me, slowly.", "If it's found: no harm done, and nothing needs saying to anyone. If it's genuinely not found, we tell your caregiver together and they help decide what to do. I never accuse anyone, and neither of us confronts anyone — that's a person's job, handled calmly.")),
        HelperDef(35, "A6", "Where is my spouse? When are they coming home?", HelperMode.AUTO_CHECK, checkKey = CheckKey.SPOUSE, triggers = listOf("where is my husband", "where is my wife", "when is she coming home", "when is he coming home", "where is my spouse"),
            steps = listOf("I'm right here with you. Would you like to look at a photo together, or hear a familiar song while we sit with this?")),
        HelperDef(36, "A6", "Nobody calls me. Nobody cares. What's the point.", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("nobody calls me", "nobody cares", "what's the point", "no one visits me"),
            steps = listOf("I'm glad you told me. I'm not going to argue with the feeling — lonely is heavy, and it isn't a failing.", "One true thing I can check: your recent calls. Sometimes a call from family happened a few days ago and it helps to hear about it again. Shall I look?", "One concrete offer, your choice: shall we call someone you like talking to now, or shall I keep you company a while?", "If you ever feel like harming yourself, or like you don't want to be alive, I will get a person — your caregiver, or 988 in the US — and I'll stay with you while we do. No secrecy about that, ever, because you matter more than a promise like that.")),
        HelperDef(37, "A6", "Evening restlessness — \"I need to go home\" / \"they're waiting for me\"", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("i need to go home", "they're waiting for me", "i have to get to work", "evening restless"),
            steps = listOf("You're thinking about home — and you are home. This is your chair, and your photos are right there. Let's have a cup of tea.", "Nobody is waiting, and nothing is due tonight. Work, errands, all of it is done for the day.", "A small familiar thing helps evenings settle: folding, music from your era, a photo album. Shall we pick one?", "If you feel you must leave the house, we call your caregiver first and I'll keep you company inside while we do.")),
        // ── A7 · Out & about ─────────────────────────────────────────
        HelperDef(38, "A7", "I can't find my car in the parking lot", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("can't find my car", "lost my car", "where did i park"),
            steps = listOf("Happens to everyone in this lot. Stay by the store entrance — we'll find it by thinking first, then walking together.", "Which door did you come in by? Cars usually sit in the row facing that door. Picture that row.", "Stay talking to me while you walk the row. If your key fob has a horn or lock button, pressing lock makes the car chirp — that's your beacon.", "Not found in about ten minutes, or you're getting distressed, or the weather's bad: we call your caregiver or the store's courtesy desk. And if you're shaken when we find it, we call for a ride first — driving can wait.")),
        HelperDef(39, "A7", "I'm at the wrong doctor's office / my appointment isn't here", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("wrong doctor's office", "appointment isn't here", "wrong office"),
            steps = listOf("The most common cause is the wrong day, not the wrong place — let's read the appointment again carefully, day spelled out.", "If it's today but at another office: if there's time, we go there together, step by step. If it's tight, we call the clinic now and say you're coming.", "If the appointment was missed entirely, we rebook by phone together, now, while it's fresh.")),
        HelperDef(40, "A7", "The bus went past / I missed my stop / I'm not sure where I am", HelperMode.AUTO_CHECK, checkKey = CheckKey.LOCATION, triggers = listOf("missed my stop", "bus went past", "not sure where i am", "i'm lost"),
            steps = listOf("Stay right where you are — don't keep walking while we sort this out.", "Read me the street sign on the corner, or a shop name. That pins the place down fast.", "Often the simplest safe plan wins: stay put and have your caregiver come to you. If you're confident and it's daytime, I'll give one instruction at a time and stay with you.")),
        HelperDef(41, "A7", "The store / pharmacy is asking something I don't understand at the counter", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("at the counter", "pharmacy counter question", "don't understand at the store"),
            steps = listOf("Repeat what they said to me, or put me on speaker, and I'll explain it. Common ones: 'generic' means the same medicine from a different maker, and it costs less. 'Prior authorization' means the pharmacy is waiting on the doctor — nothing for you to do.", "If a signature screen appears, you can always say: 'Please print that so my family can read it.' That's allowed everywhere.", "Anything asking for your full Social Security number, or a new loyalty account with a fee: 'No thank you, not today' is the whole answer.")),
        HelperDef(42, "A7", "My car is making a noise / a light came on / it won't start", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("car won't start", "car making a noise", "warning light on", "car light came on"),
            steps = listOf("For a car that won't start, three safe checks: is it in Park? Is your foot on the brake? And what does it do when you turn the key — a click, silence, or cranking?", "A single click with dim lights is usually the battery. The answer is a helper call, not turning the key again and again.", "If you're driving and a red light comes on, or there's steam or a new loud noise: pull into the next safe place, engine off, hazard lights on — then we call your caregiver or roadside help. I never declare a car safe to drive; that's a person on the scene.")),
        HelperDef(43, "A7", "I locked my keys in the car / house", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("locked my keys", "keys in the car", "locked out"),
            steps = listOf("Nothing is ruined — keys are the most locked-in thing in America.", "We follow the household plan: call the person who has the spare. If there's no spare plan, we call roadside help or a locksmith together — using the number on your insurance card or from your caregiver, never a random ad found under stress.", "If a child or a pet is locked in a hot car, that's 911 immediately — the dispatcher's guidance comes first. Otherwise, find shade and water if it's hot, and I'll stay with you while we wait.")),
        // ── A8 · Visitors, deliveries & household services ───────────
        HelperDef(44, "A8", "A package says delivered, but it's not at my door", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("package not here", "says delivered but", "missing package"),
            steps = listOf("The usual places, in order: side door, by the garage, behind the planter, and with a neighbor — carriers leave things at the wrong house often.", "'Delivered' sometimes means it's at the local station and coming tomorrow. Let's read any delivery note together — show me with 'Show Nuri'.", "Still missing after a day? The report is a call to the store — I'll draft what to say. And if a 'delivered' text arrived with a link or a fee, that's a scam pattern, not a delivery.")),
        HelperDef(45, "A8", "Someone is coming today — or are they? I forget", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("is someone coming today", "cleaner coming", "who is coming today", "visitor today"),
            steps = listOf("If nobody was expected today, that's useful to know plainly: anyone at the door today is a surprise, and surprises can wait.", "When someone IS expected, the helpful facts are their name, the time, and what they'll do — ask me again any time and I'll repeat them exactly.")),
        HelperDef(46, "A8", "The meal / grocery delivery is missing things / never came", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("groceries missing", "delivery missing items", "food delivery never came"),
            steps = listOf("First, the door spots — side door, garage, planter — like a package.", "Now the receipt against the bag: show me the receipt with 'Show Nuri' and we'll name what's missing, plainly.", "The fix is a phone call with a simple script: 'Two things are missing from my order.' I'll stay with you while you call. If the app confuses, the phone call is the path — saying so is the help.")),
        // ── A9 · Pets ────────────────────────────────────────────────
        HelperDef(47, "A9", "The dog got out", HelperMode.ESCALATE, triggers = listOf("dog got out", "the dog escaped", "dog ran away"),
            steps = listOf("Stay at the house — dogs come back to home, and if you go searching we'd have two to find. Open the gate and put his blanket by the door.", "We tell your caregiver and a neighbor right now, with his description. Use the 'Ask' button here and I'll mark it urgent in the diary — and if you can, call them too.", "If he's spotted near a road, that's a person-goes task, not yours. Stay home; home is his target.")),
        HelperDef(48, "A9", "Did anyone feed the cat? / The dog ate something bad", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("did anyone feed", "dog ate something", "cat ate something", "dog ate chocolate"),
            steps = listOf("Feeding first: if we keep a feeding record, I'll answer from it. If it's uncertain, your household's setup rule decides — a small half-portion is the common one — I state the rule, I don't invent it.", "Ate something bad is different — that's urgent and it's a vet question right now. No home remedies, no waiting to see: we call the vet or your caregiver now, especially for chocolate, grapes, sugar-free gum, or any medicine.")),
        // ── A10 · Change & disruption ────────────────────────────────
        HelperDef(49, "A10", "Everything is different — new phone / moved room / things gone", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("everything is different", "new phone confusion", "my things are gone", "room moved"),
            steps = listOf("Let's name the change plainly first — a new phone, a moved room — because unexplained change feels worse than explained change.", "Your numbers and photos came with you. Let's rebuild one anchor at a time: the call you make most, together, right now.", "Ask me the same question tomorrow and I'll answer it the same way. Anchors come back one at a time.")),
        HelperDef(50, "A10", "Home from hospital — everything is overwhelming / the pill list changed", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("home from hospital", "discharge papers", "pill list changed", "hospital list"),
            steps = listOf("Welcome home. The discharge papers are the source of truth for the next days — keep them on the counter, and show them to me with 'Show Nuri' whenever you want them read aloud.", "If the hospital list and your old bottles differ, I can point out the differences — one list has a new one, one old one is missing. I never decide which list wins.", "Before the next dose, we call the pharmacist or the doctor's office together and read both lists. And your caregiver hears about today the same day — coming home is a high-confusion window, and that's expected, not a failing.")),
        HelperDef(51, "A10", "The clocks changed / family visiting / my routine is all wrong today", HelperMode.GUIDED, triggers = listOf("routine is wrong", "clocks changed", "family visiting", "holiday confusion"),
            steps = listOf("Let's name why today is different, so it stops feeling like you're wrong: a holiday, visitors, a clock change — the day changed, not you.", "Your anchors still hold inside it: your chair, your room, your evening show. And one quiet period is yours whenever you want it.", "When the guests go home, tomorrow is a normal day again. Nothing is expected of you beyond being here.")),
